{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And when he would let down his hand</b> — On the plain sense, when he let his hand down under duress because of the heaviness of his hands, he saw that Amalek prevailed, and he commanded Aaron and Hur to support them so that he would not let them down any more. And our Sages said in the Midrash (Sefer haBahir §138): \"Was Moses then doing something to cause Amalek to prevail over him? Rather, a person is forbidden to keep his hands spread out toward heaven for three hours.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:09:41.059415835Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}